meta {
  name: Simplespace Delete Space
  type: http
  seq: 150
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.simplespace.deleteSpace
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "space": "at://{{did}}/space/org.example.bucket/main"
  }
}

docs {
  Delete a simplespace space. The space row stays as a tombstone (getSpaceCredential keeps
  answering SpaceDeleted, the durable deletion signal for syncers), its config and member
  list are cleared, and the authority's own repo in the space is deleted with it. Other
  members' repos are not erased — their records are theirs — they simply stop being
  readable or writable. Idempotent: deleting again is a 200. The URI may later be
  created again.

  Requires a "space:…?manage=delete" grant and the caller must be the space's authority.
  Errors: 400 SpaceNotFound when the space never existed, 400 NotSpaceOwner,
  403 InsufficientScope.
}
